// DISABLED: performance.simpleperf.SimplePerfTest
//
// Its client was moved to test/disabled/performance/simpleperf/counterClient.java,
// but this entry and performance/simpleperf/SimplePerfTest.java were left behind, so
// the test still ran and failed with
//
//   java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: performance.simpleperf.counterClient
//
// (SimplePerfTest names the client as a string, via createClient(...), which is why
// nothing failed to compile.)
//
// It cannot simply be moved back. That client benchmarks the servant-caching POA
// variants using the ORB's timer subsystem, and that subsystem is gone: there is no
// com.sun.corba.ee.impl.orbutil.newtimer.generated.TimingPoints any more, and
// makeTimerManager is commented out in both ORBImpl and ORBSingleton. Restoring it
// means deleting the timing instrumentation that is the only reason it differs from
// simpleperf2 below - which measures the same local/RMI-IIOP invocation cost and passes.
//
// @disabled(its counterClient was moved to test/disabled - see the note above) -test performance.simpleperf.SimplePerfTest

-test performance.simpleperf2.SimplePerfTest
